- second item
```

#2 Full names and compact aliases

Block directives support canonical names and official short aliases. Both forms produce the same AST, so you can choose clarity for public documents or speed while drafting.

```sm
&note [title="A note"]
This is the full form.
&end

&n [title="A note"]
This is the equivalent compact form.
&e
```

| Canonical form | Compact form | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `&note` ... `&end` | `&n` ... `&e` | General note |
| `&test` ... `&end` | `&t` ... `&e` | Test / typing block |
| `&warning` ... `&end` | `&w` ... `&e` | Warning |

Both `&name[attrs]` and `&name [attrs]` are valid. A valueless attribute means `true`, for example `[typing]`.

#2 Parse and render

```typescript
import { parseDocument, renderHtml } from "structmark-language-core";

const document = parseDocument(source);
const html = renderHtml(document);
```

`parseDocument` only parses the source. It does not execute code or access the network or filesystem.

